From: aiueo52 <aiueo52@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 13:19:58 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 044/105] mtp entry: precompute the embedding-side projection
 per token (SGLANG_MTP_EMBED_TABLE)

The Qwen4-Exp MTP entry fusion adds fc_embedding(pre_fc_norm_embedding(
embed_tokens(id))) to fc_hidden(pre_fc_norm_hidden(hidden)). The first term
depends only on the token id and on weights that never change after load, yet
the draft recomputes it on every iteration -- 15 times per decode step at W16,
3 at W4, plus draft_extend.

SGLANG_MTP_EMBED_TABLE=1 materialises that term for the whole vocabulary once
the embedding tensor is real (`set_embed_and_head`, or the end of a standalone
`load_weights`), and the draft then replaces the gather + norm + GEMM with a
single gather. The full table fits (248320 x 2560 bf16 = 1.18 GB), so there is
no hot-id/cold-id split and no fallback branch: the reduced draft vocabulary
(--speculative-token-map) constrains only the draft's *output* ids, while the
first token of each chain comes from the target and can be anything.

Rows are filled one at a time through the same call decode makes, because
cuBLAS switches kernel -- and therefore low-order bits -- with M; a batched
build is not bit-identical to the M=1 kernel a bs=1 draft step runs. The norm
is a per-row reduction and stays batched. A post-build check compares 256
random rows against the live path and drops the table if any differ, so an
unexpected dispatch can only cost the optimisation, never correctness.

Measured on Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVFP4 (same session, flag off vs on):

  W16  draft busy 5.00/4.98 -> 4.76/4.72 ms/step, 745 -> 717 kernels
  W4   draft busy 0.62/0.61 -> 0.59/0.58 ms/step, 119 -> 115 kernels

  internal::gemvx::kernel [320,1,1]  14.0 -> 0.0 /step (-166 us) at W16
                                      2.0 -> 0.0 /step  (-24 us) at W4
  entry RMSNorm [1,1,1]              28.0 -> 14.0 /step (-31 us) at W16
                                      5.0 ->  2.0 /step  (-7 us) at W4

Build takes 2.2-2.8 s and reports 256/256 sampled rows bit-identical
(max|diff| 0.000e+00). Acceptance and needle are unchanged: W16 code-edit
10.49 / prose-en 3.02 / agent-loop 4.66, W4 3.91 / 2.49 / 3.04, needle PASS
on both.

The table is allocated after the KV pool is sized, so it comes out of the
leftover headroom: at W4 the stock --mem-fraction-static 0.96 leaves only
2.12 GB after capture and an 18.5k-token prefill then OOMs. Serving with the
flag needs the fraction lowered by ~0.013 (W4: MEM_FRACTION=0.947 restores
3.2-3.3 GB, matching the flag-off baseline); W16's 0.945 already has room
(4.42 -> 3.40 GB). SGLANG_MTP_EMBED_TABLE_RESERVE_GB raises the free-memory
floor below which the build is skipped.

